## 1. Executive Summary

In commit `1f7dd12`, `gcp-mcp-project` replaced regional Artifact Registry references (`${_REGION}-docker.pkg.dev/$PROJECT_ID/cloud-run-images/gcp-mcp:$COMMIT_SHA`) with the legacy Google Container Registry (`gcr.io/$PROJECT_ID/gcp-mcp:$COMMIT_SHA`). This hotfix bypassed permission denials triggered by strict enterprise Organization Policies (`constraints/gcp.resourceLocations`, restrictive IAM boundary constraints, and unprovisioned regional repositories in EU zones).

While resolving immediate build-pipeline blockage, this change directly perturbs four foundational system invariants:
1. **Supply-Chain & Cryptographic Attestation Invariants:** Loss of native Artifact Registry fine-grained IAM, SBOM generation, Vulnerability Scanning (Container Analysis v2), and Binary Authorization enforcement.
