## 5. Offline Synchronization, Caching, and Ingestion Queues

To prevent downstream data starvation and memory leaks during connector outages or traffic surges, ingestion is decoupled via BullMQ + Redis Stream buffers.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Webhook as External Webhook (Shopify/GA4)
    participant API as CAIP Webhook Controller
    participant Redis as Redis Buffer / BullMQ
    participant Worker as Background Ingestion Worker
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (Prisma)
    participant Casey as Casey Campaign Agent

    Webhook->>API: POST /api/webhooks/:source
    API->>API: Validate Signature & Sanitize Schema
    alt Validation Failed
        API-->>Webhook: 400 Bad Request (Drop Immediately)
    else Validation Passed
        API->>Redis: Enqueue Job (Payload + Idempotency Key)
        API-->>Webhook: 202 Accepted (Fast Ack < 25ms)
    end

