---

## 1. Executive Summary

The transition of the **CAIP (Customer AI Intelligence Platform)** backend from TypeScript to native ECMAScript Modules (ESM JavaScript) eliminates compilation latency, simplifies container builds (`Dockerfile`), and improves dynamic runtime plugin extensibility. However, eliminating static compile-time type verification shifts the entire burden of **system invariant enforcement** onto the runtime execution layer.

This RFC conducts an internal biomorphic deliberation between the **Generative Dreamer** (Default Mode Network, exploring runtime malleability and dynamic agentic routing) and the **Evaluative Arbiter** (Prefrontal Zeno Critic, evaluating failure modes, event payload drift, and probabilistic identity graph corruption). It defines the concrete architectural contracts, validation barriers, offline caching mechanisms, and safety bounds required to preserve CAIP's core guarantees in a JavaScript-native runtime.

```mermaid
