### 2.1 Comparative Contract Matrix

| Invariant Dimension | Pre-PR #19 State (`getAllUsers`) | Post-PR #19 Target State (`listUsers`) | Downstream Impact & Risk |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **API Semantic Contract** | Ambiguous: implied full collection dump ($O(N)$). | Bounded: structured pagination envelope ($O(\min(N, K))$). | Downstream parsers expecting raw arrays will break without envelope unwrapping. |
| **Database Execution** | Full table scan / unbounded `SELECT *` under high concurrency. | Bounded `LIMIT`/`OFFSET` (migrating to Keyset Cursors). | Prevents database CPU/IOPS starvation; requires composite indexing. |
| **Memory Footprint** | Unbounded heap allocation during large user dataset serialization. | Constant $O(K)$ buffer allocation per request. | Eliminates Node.js V8 heap starvation and GC thrashing. |
| **Cache Key Topology** | Monolithic cache keys (`users:all`). | Granular parametrized composite keys (`users:list:hash(params)`). | Granular invalidation; avoids invalidating the entire user directory on single update. |
| **Gateway Rate Limiting** | Coarse endpoint rate limiting. | Fine-grained cost-weighted rate limiting based on page size. | Prevents API Gateway DoS via high-page-count scraping. |

