```
PHASE 1: Internal Refactor (PR #19 - Complete)
├── Controller, Service, and Unit Tests standardized to listUsers.

PHASE 2: Invariant Hardening & Keyset Migration (Current Target)
├── Introduce HMAC Cursor encoding/decoding.
├── Apply composite PostgreSQL indices concurrently.
├── Configure Kong API Gateway parameter clamping (max pageSize = 100).

PHASE 3: Downstream Client Migration & Deprecation Monitoring
├── Update application-service and analytics-service client SDKs.
├── Monitor ELK logs for calls to legacy getAllUsers aliases.
├── Track Prometheus metrics: `http_requests_total{handler="listUsers"}`.

PHASE 4: Final Deprecation
└── Sunset legacy getAllUsers routing and database offset shims.
```

### 8.1 Observability Metrics (Prometheus / ELK)
* `user_service_list_duration_seconds{quantile="0.99"}`: Must remain $< 35\text{ms}$.
* `user_service_list_cache_hit_ratio`: Target $> 85\%$.
* `user_service_invalid_cursor_attempts_total`: Security alarm if $> 10/\text{min}$.

---

## 9. Conclusion
Merge pull request #19 represents the necessary first step in elevating the `ai-platform` user domain from an unstructured monolith pattern to an enterprise-grade MACH microservice. Adopting the keyset pagination, multi-tier caching, and cryptographic cursor specifications detailed in this RFC guarantees predictable latencies, zero downtime, and robust invariant safety as the platform scales.

