# RFC: CDP_REALTIME_STEWARDSHIP

**Title:** Lock-Free Real-Time Customer Identity Graph Reconciliation via Monotonic Graph CRDTs and Wait-Free Disjoint Forests  
**Status:** Proposed  
**Author:** Core Architecture & Cognitive Systems Engineering  
**Target Subsystem:** `customer-mdm` (Core Stewardship & Real-time CDC Engine)  
**Target Repository:** `/workspace/customer-mdm`  
**Classification:** Core Data Architecture / High-Throughput Streaming Engine  

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Problem Statement

### 1.1 The Operational Bottleneck
In traditional Customer Master Data Management (CDP/MDM) platforms, streaming Change Data Capture (CDC) pipelines (e.g., Debezium tailing PostgreSQL, MongoDB, or ERP databases) face a severe throughput and concurrency wall during identity resolution:
1. **Pessimistic Locking (`SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`):** Merging customer profiles across multiple concurrent CDC events (e.g., web clickstreams, checkout events, CRM updates) forces distributed locks across customer records and their adjacency lists, inducing lock contention, deadlocks, and cascading backpressure.
2. **Split-Brain & Ordering Hazards:** Distributed streaming pipelines partition traffic across multiple Kafka/Redpanda partitions. Out-of-order delivery causes non-deterministic cluster convergence and race conditions during simultaneous merge/split operations.
3. **The Unmerge / Split Asymmetry:** While merging is computationally cheap (graph edge insertion), splitting/unmerging an erroneous merge requires re-evaluating connected components across the graph. In a locked relational schema, an unmerge locks entire subgraphs, halting real-time ingestion.

### 1.2 Proposed Paradigm
This RFC outlines an architecture for **Lock-Free Real-Time Identity Graph Reconciliation**. It eliminates distributed mutual exclusion by framing the identity graph as a **Monotonic Add-Wins Observed-Remove Graph Conflict-Free Replicated Data Type (AWOR-Graph CRDT)** layered on top of an in-memory **Wait-Free Concurrent Disjoint-Set (Union-Find) with Atomic Compare-And-Swap (CAS)**.

```
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                REAL-TIME INGESTION PIPELINE                                 |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
   CDC Stream (Kafka/Redpanda)
        │
        ▼
   Consistent Hashing Router (Murmur3 over Entity Keys)
        │
        ▼
   Entropy & Hub Gating (Shannon Entropy Filter / Blacklist Bloom Filter)
        │
        ├── [Entropy Violation / Hub Detected] ──────► Quarantine Queue / Manual Stewardship
        │
        ▼
   In-Memory Wait-Free AWOR-Graph Engine (CAS Path-Compression Union-Find)
        │
        ├── Concurrent Merge ────► Atomic CAS Edge Linking + Lattice Join (⊔)
        └── Concurrent Split ────► Edge Tombstone + Bounded Incremental Radius Recalculation
        │
        ▼
   Deterministic Golden Record Reducer (Pure Functional Survivorship)
        │
        ▼
   Materialized View (RocksDB / Redis Tier-1 Cache & Downstream Kafka Topic)
```

---

## 2. Theoretical Model & Data Structures

### 2.1 Hybrid Logical Clocks (HLC) & Graph Elements
Every CDC identity assertion edge is stamped with a Hybrid Logical Clock $HLC = (l, c)$ where $l$ is physical wall time and $c$ is a logical counter, guaranteeing causal and total ordering without central clock synchronization.

```typescript
export type NodeID = string; // e.g., "email:user@domain.com", "crm:109482", "cookie:anon_9f81"
export type ClusterID = string; // Canonical identifier for the unified golden profile

export interface HLCTimestamp {
  wallTime: number; // Unix epoch milliseconds
  logical: number;  // Monotonic sequence counter for ties
  nodeId: string;   // Disambiguation tie-breaker
}

export interface IdentityNode {
  id: NodeID;
  type: 'EMAIL' | 'PHONE' | 'DEVICE_ID' | 'CRM_ID' | 'COOKIE' | 'NATIONAL_ID';
  attributes: Record<string, unknown>;
  createdAt: HLCTimestamp;
  updatedAt: HLCTimestamp;
}

export interface IdentityEdge {
  id: string; // Deterministic: SHA256(min(source, target) + ":" + max(source, target) + ":" + context)
  source: NodeID;
  target: NodeID;
  confidenceScore: number; // [0.0 - 1.0]
  ruleId: string;
  sourceSystem: string;
  hlc: HLCTimestamp;
  tombstoned: boolean;
}
```

### 2.2 Monotonic AWOR-Graph Lattice
Let $G = (V, E)$ be the customer graph. The identity state is defined as a join-semilattice $L = (S, \sqcup)$ where state $S = (V_{add}, V_{rem}, E_{add}, E_{rem})$:

$$E_{active} = \{ e \in E_{add} \mid \forall r \in E_{rem}. (e.id = r.id \implies e.hlc > r.hlc) \}$$

The merge operator $(\sqcup)$ for two graph replicas $S_1$ and $S_2$ computes the set union of additions and removals independently:

$$S_1 \sqcup S_2 = (V_{add1} \cup V_{add2}, \; V_{rem1} \cup V_{rem2}, \; E_{add1} \cup E_{add2}, \; E_{rem1} \cup E_{rem2})$$

Because set union is associative, commutative, and idempotent ($A \cup A = A$), any CDC replica converges deterministically without distributed locks.

---

## 3. Core Algorithms

### 3.1 Lock-Free Concurrent Disjoint-Set (Union-Find)
To query the canonical root (`ClusterID`) of an identifier in $O(\alpha(N))$ time without mutexes, we employ Jayanti's atomic CAS path-halving algorithm.

```typescript
export class AtomicDisjointSet {
  // Maps NodeID -> Atomic Reference to Parent NodeID
  private parent: Map<NodeID, string> = new Map();
  // Maps NodeID -> Rank for tree balance
  private rank: Map<NodeID, number> = new Map();

  public find(node: NodeID): NodeID {
    let curr = node;
    if (!this.parent.has(curr)) {
      this.parent.set(curr, curr);
      this.rank.set(curr, 0);
      return curr;
    }

    // Lock-free path halving with atomic pointers
    while (true) {
      const p = this.parent.get(curr)!;
      const gp = this.parent.get(p) ?? p;
      if (p === gp) {
        return p;
      }
      // CAS step to compress path: curr.parent = gp
      this.parent.set(curr, gp);
      curr = gp;
    }
  }

  public union(nodeA: NodeID, nodeB: NodeID): NodeID {
    while (true) {
      const rootA = this.find(nodeA);
      const rootB = this.find(nodeB);

      if (rootA === rootB) return rootA;

      const rankA = this.rank.get(rootA) || 0;
      const rankB = this.rank.get(rootB) || 0;

      // Deterministic parent selection based on rank, then lexical ID
      let newRoot: NodeID;
      let child: NodeID;

      if (rankA < rankB) {
        newRoot = rootB;
        child = rootA;
      } else if (rankA > rankB) {
        newRoot = rootA;
        child = rootB;
      } else {
        // Equal rank: break tie lexically for strict determinism across nodes
        newRoot = rootA < rootB ? rootA : rootB;
        child = rootA < rootB ? rootB : rootA;
        this.rank.set(newRoot, rankA + 1);
      }

      // Atomic pointer swap: child.parent = newRoot
      const prevParent = this.parent.get(child);
      if (prevParent === child) {
        this.parent.set(child, newRoot);
        return newRoot;
      }
      // If another thread modified child.parent, loop retries automatically
    }
  }
}
```

---

### 3.2 Real-Time CDC Ingestion & Identity Reconciliation
When a CDC event arrives, the engine performs atomic validation, entropy filtering, and edge assimilation.

```typescript
export class IdentityReconciliationEngine {
  private disjointSet = new AtomicDisjointSet();
  private edgeStore: Map<string, IdentityEdge> = new Map();
  private nodeAdjacency: Map<NodeID, Set<string>> = new Map(); // NodeID -> Set of EdgeIDs
  private blacklist: Set<string> = new Set(); // Pre-compiled Bloom/Exact filter for junk identifiers
  private static readonly DEGREE_THRESHOLD = 50; // Guard against mega-hub corruption

  /**
   * Evaluates incoming CDC link assertion without acquiring DB locks.
   */
  public reconcileIdentityDelta(
    sourceNode: IdentityNode,
    targetNode: IdentityNode,
    edgePayload: IdentityEdge
  ): { clusterId: ClusterID; isQuarantined: boolean; status: string } {
    // 1. Blacklist & Universal Identifier Sanitization
    if (this.isBlacklisted(sourceNode.id) || this.isBlacklisted(targetNode.id)) {
      return { clusterId: '', isQuarantined: true, status: 'REJECTED_BLACKLIST' };
    }

    // 2. High-Degree Hub Protection (Entropy Gating)
    if (this.violatesDegreeLimit(sourceNode.id) || this.violatesDegreeLimit(targetNode.id)) {
      return { clusterId: '', isQuarantined: true, status: 'QUARANTINED_HIGH_DEGREE_HUB' };
    }

    // 3. CRDT Edge LWW Reconciliation
    const existingEdge = this.edgeStore.get(edgePayload.id);
    if (existingEdge && this.compareHLC(existingEdge.hlc, edgePayload.hlc) >= 0) {
      // Inbound event is older or equal to local state; discard out-of-order event
      const currentRoot = this.disjointSet.find(sourceNode.id);
      return { clusterId: currentRoot, isQuarantined: false, status: 'NOOP_STALE_EVENT' };
    }

    // 4. Ingest Edge into State Store
    this.edgeStore.set(edgePayload.id, edgePayload);
    this.registerAdjacency(edgePayload.source, edgePayload.id);
    this.registerAdjacency(edgePayload.target, edgePayload.id);

    if (edgePayload.tombstoned) {
      // Trigger non-blocking topological split re-evaluation
      const newCluster = this.handleEdgeRetraction(edgePayload);
      return { clusterId: newCluster, isQuarantined: false, status: 'SPLIT_PROCESSED' };
    }

    // 5. Lock-free Union Execution
    const canonicalCluster = this.disjointSet.union(sourceNode.id, targetNode.id);

    return {
      clusterId: canonicalCluster,
      isQuarantined: false,
      status: 'MERGED_SUCCESSFULLY'
    };
  }

  private isBlacklisted(id: string): boolean {
    const rawVal = id.split(':')[1]?.toLowerCase() || '';
    return (
      this.blacklist.has(id) ||
      rawVal === '000-00-0000' ||
      rawVal === 'null' ||
      rawVal === 'undefined' ||
      rawVal === 'unknown@domain.com' ||
      rawVal === 'test@test.com'
    );
  }

  private violatesDegreeLimit(nodeId: NodeID): boolean {
    const adj = this.nodeAdjacency.get(nodeId);
    return adj ? adj.size >= IdentityReconciliationEngine.DEGREE_THRESHOLD : false;
  }

  private registerAdjacency(nodeId: NodeID, edgeId: string): void {
    let edges = this.nodeAdjacency.get(nodeId);
    if (!edges) {
      edges = new Set<string>();
      this.nodeAdjacency.set(nodeId, edges);
    }
    edges.add(edgeId);
  }

  private compareHLC(a: HLCTimestamp, b: HLCTimestamp): number {
    if (a.wallTime !== b.wallTime) return a.wallTime - b.wallTime;
    if (a.logical !== b.logical) return a.logical - b.logical;
    return a.nodeId.localeCompare(b.nodeId);
  }

  /**
   * Asynchronous/Non-blocking Split Handler using bounded local graph traversal.
   */
  private handleEdgeRetraction(retractedEdge: IdentityEdge): ClusterID {
    // 1. Remove edge from active adjacency
    this.nodeAdjacency.get(retractedEdge.source)?.delete(retractedEdge.id);
    this.nodeAdjacency.get(retractedEdge.target)?.delete(retractedEdge.id);

    // 2. Re-evaluate reachability between source and target via bounded bidirectional BFS
    const isStillConnected = this.checkReachability(
      retractedEdge.source,
      retractedEdge.target,
      1000 // Bounded depth/step limit
    );

    if (isStillConnected) {
      // Redundant paths exist; identity graph remains connected
      return this.disjointSet.find(retractedEdge.source);
    }

    // 3. Components have split: Re-seed disjoint forest locally for the affected sub-components
    return this.rebuildSubcomponent(retractedEdge.source);
  }

  private checkReachability(start: NodeID, target: NodeID, maxSteps: number): boolean {
    const visited = new Set<NodeID>();
    const queue: NodeID[] = [start];
    let steps = 0;

    while (queue.length > 0 && steps < maxSteps) {
      steps++;
      const curr = queue.shift()!;
      if (curr === target) return true;
      visited.add(curr);

      const edgeIds = this.nodeAdjacency.get(curr) || [];
      for (const edgeId of edgeIds) {
        const edge = this.edgeStore.get(edgeId);
        if (!edge || edge.tombstoned) continue;
        const neighbor = edge.source === curr ? edge.target : edge.source;
        if (!visited.has(neighbor)) {
          queue.push(neighbor);
        }
      }
    }
    return false;
  }

  private rebuildSubcomponent(originNode: NodeID): ClusterID {
    // Reconstruct local connected component and assign updated cluster ID
    const visited = new Set<NodeID>();
    const queue: NodeID[] = [originNode];
    let canonicalRoot = originNode;

    while (queue.length > 0) {
      const curr = queue.shift()!;
      visited.add(curr);
      if (curr < canonicalRoot) canonicalRoot = curr; // Lexical canonicalization

      const edgeIds = this.nodeAdjacency.get(curr) || [];
      for (const edgeId of edgeIds) {
        const edge = this.edgeStore.get(edgeId);
        if (!edge || edge.tombstoned) continue;
        const neighbor = edge.source === curr ? edge.target : edge.source;
        if (!visited.has(neighbor)) {
          queue.push(neighbor);
        }
      }
    }
    return canonicalRoot;
  }
}
```

---

## 4. Deterministic Golden Record Selection

Once the identity graph converges, the **Golden Record** is materialized without querying external databases by executing a pure-functional reduction over the active component nodes.

### 4.1 Survivorship Specification
```
                  +-----------------------------------+
                  |   Active Cluster Node Subgraph    |
                  +-----------------------------------+
                                    │
                                    ▼
       ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │ Field-Level Survivorship Reducer:                           │
       │                                                             │
       │ 1. Source Trust Hierarchy (ERP > CRM > Web Form > Cookie)  │
       │ 2. Recency Tie-Breaking (Max HLC Timestamp)                 │
       │ 3. Frequency / Agreement Voting (Consensus fields)          │
       │ 4. Completeness Scoring (Length / Non-null check)           │
       └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                    │
                                    ▼
                  +-----------------------------------+
                  | Unified Golden Customer Profile   |
                  +-----------------------------------+
```

```typescript
export interface CustomerAttribute<T> {
  value: T;
  source: string;
  hlc: HLCTimestamp;
}

export interface UnifiedGoldenProfile {
  clusterId: ClusterID;
  canonicalEmail: string;
  canonicalPhone: string;
  firstName: string;
  lastName: string;
  allAssociatedIdentifiers: NodeID[];
  lineageVersion: number;
}

export class GoldenRecordReducer {
  private static SOURCE_WEIGHTS: Record<string, number> = {
    ERP: 100,
    CRM: 80,
    MOBILE_APP: 60,
    WEB_CHECKOUT: 50,
    MARKETING_COOKIE: 10
  };

  public static reduce(clusterId: ClusterID, nodes: IdentityNode[]): UnifiedGoldenProfile {
    const emails: CustomerAttribute<string>[] = [];
    const phones: CustomerAttribute<string>[] = [];
    const firstNames: CustomerAttribute<string>[] = [];
    const lastNames: CustomerAttribute<string>[] = [];

    for (const node of nodes) {
      if (node.attributes.email) {
        emails.push({
          value: String(node.attributes.email),
          source: String(node.attributes.sourceSystem || 'WEB_CHECKOUT'),
          hlc: node.updatedAt
        });
      }
      if (node.attributes.phone) {
        phones.push({
          value: String(node.attributes.phone),
          source: String(node.attributes.sourceSystem || 'WEB_CHECKOUT'),
          hlc: node.updatedAt
        });
      }
      if (node.attributes.firstName) {
        firstNames.push({
          value: String(node.attributes.firstName),
          source: String(node.attributes.sourceSystem || 'WEB_CHECKOUT'),
          hlc: node.updatedAt
        });
      }
      if (node.attributes.lastName) {
        lastNames.push({
          value: String(node.attributes.lastName),
          source: String(node.attributes.sourceSystem || 'WEB_CHECKOUT'),
          hlc: node.updatedAt
        });
      }
    }

    return {
      clusterId,
      canonicalEmail: this.selectWinningAttribute(emails),
      canonicalPhone: this.selectWinningAttribute(phones),
      firstName: this.selectWinningAttribute(firstNames),
      lastName: this.selectWinningAttribute(lastNames),
      allAssociatedIdentifiers: nodes.map(n => n.id),
      lineageVersion: Date.now()
    };
  }

  private static selectWinningAttribute(candidates: CustomerAttribute<string>[]): string {
    if (candidates.length === 0) return '';
    return candidates.sort((a, b) => {
      const weightA = this.SOURCE_WEIGHTS[a.source] || 0;
      const weightB = this.SOURCE_WEIGHTS[b.source] || 0;
      if (weightA !== weightB) return weightB - weightA; // Higher source priority wins
      if (a.hlc.wallTime !== b.hlc.wallTime) return b.hlc.wallTime - a.hlc.wallTime; // More recent wins
      return a.value.localeCompare(b.value); // Deterministic string tie-break
    })[0].value;
  }
}
```

---

## 5. Offline Sync, Caching & Memory Tiering

```
+─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────+
| MEMORY HIERARCHY & PERSISTENCE TIERS                                    |
+─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────+
| Tier 1: L1 In-Memory Lock-Free Union-Find (CAS Pointer Array)           |
|         - Sub-microsecond cluster ID resolution                         |
|         - JVM / V8 Off-heap direct memory mapped buffer                 |
+─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────+
| Tier 2: L2 Embedded LSM-Tree (RocksDB on NVMe)                          |
|         - Column Families: [GraphEdges], [NodeAttributes], [HLCIndex]   |
|         - Point lookup: ~15µs; Append-only WAL for crash recovery       |
+─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────+
| Tier 3: Cold Lineage & Audit Archive (Parquet on Cloud Object Store)   |
|         - Hourly compacted delta snapshots                              |
|         - Immutable audit trail for compliance & GDPR Right-to-Forget   |
+─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────+
```

### 5.1 Tombstone Compaction & Garbage Collection
Tombstones generated by split operations are retained for $T_{quarantine} = 7 \text{ days}$ (to handle deep out-of-order CDC replay) and subsequently compacted during background LSM compaction windows.

---

## 6. Edge Cases, Failure Modes & Safety Bounds

| Failure Mode | Impact | Mitigation Strategy |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **High-Degree Mega Hub** *(e.g., call center phone, placeholder email)* | Millions of identities collapse into a single cluster. | **Entropy Gating & Dynamic Degree Clamping:** Nodes with vertex degree $k > 50$ or Shannon Entropy $H(X) < 1.5$ are instantly isolated into quarantine and alerted to data stewards. |
| **Out-of-Order CDC Arrival** | Stale update overwrites fresh link data. | **Strict HLC Monotonicity:** Inbound deltas with $HLC_{in} \le HLC_{stored}$ are discarded as idempotent no-ops. |
| **Cascading Unmerge (Chain Split)** | Edge deletion triggers recursive split across 100k nodes. | **Bounded Local Bi-directional BFS:** Depth-limited to $R_{max} = 1000$ steps. Beyond this bound, async worker pools recalculate subgraphs via offloaded MapReduce jobs. |
| **Split-Brain Network Partition** | Ingestion worker nodes process disjoint partition segments. | **Consistent Partition Routing:** Kafka keys hashed over `canonical_anchor_id` guarantee all edges for an entity land on the same stream processor instance. |
| **GDPR "Right to be Forgotten"** | Graph node deletion required by law. | **Tombstone Insertion + Selective Lineage Pruning:** Target node emits a high-priority erasure tombstone with $HLC = \infty$, purging attributes and severing connected edges. |

---

## 7. Migration & Rollout Plan

1. **Phase 1 (Shadow Pipeline - Weeks 1-2):** Deploy streaming AWOR-Graph engine in shadow mode alongside legacy MDM. Mirror CDC streams from Kafka and measure convergence consistency via automated diff assertions.
2. **Phase 2 (Read-Path Decoupling - Weeks 3-4):** Route downstream CDP lookup APIs (`/v1/customer/360`) to the RocksDB Tier-1 Materialized Cache.
3. **Phase 3 (Full Cutover & Legacy Deprecation - Week 5):** Disable legacy relational row-level locking schemas and transition fully to the wait-free CDC reconciliation topology.

---

## 8. Verification & Test Harness

```typescript
describe('IdentityReconciliationEngine Concurrency & CRDT Properties', () => {
  let engine: IdentityReconciliationEngine;

  beforeEach(() => {
    engine = new IdentityReconciliationEngine();
  });

  test('Convergence under out-of-order event delivery (Commutativity)', () => {
    const nodeA: IdentityNode = { id: 'email:alice@domain.com', type: 'EMAIL', attributes: {}, createdAt: { wallTime: 100, logical: 0, nodeId: 'n1' }, updatedAt: { wallTime: 100, logical: 0, nodeId: 'n1' } };
    const nodeB: IdentityNode = { id: 'crm:alice_99', type: 'CRM_ID', attributes: {}, createdAt: { wallTime: 105, logical: 0, nodeId: 'n1' }, updatedAt: { wallTime: 105, logical: 0, nodeId: 'n1' } };

    const edge: IdentityEdge = {
      id: 'edge_a_b',
      source: nodeA.id,
      target: nodeB.id,
      confidenceScore: 0.99,
      ruleId: 'EXACT_MATCH',
      sourceSystem: 'CRM',
      hlc: { wallTime: 110, logical: 1, nodeId: 'nodeA' },
      tombstoned: false
    };

    const staleEdge: IdentityEdge = {
      ...edge,
      hlc: { wallTime: 102, logical: 0, nodeId: 'nodeA' },
      confidenceScore: 0.50
    };

    // Deliver fresh edge first, then stale edge
    const res1 = engine.reconcileIdentityDelta(nodeA, nodeB, edge);
    const res2 = engine.reconcileIdentityDelta(nodeA, nodeB, staleEdge);

    expect(res1.status).toBe('MERGED_SUCCESSFULLY');
    expect(res2.status).toBe('NOOP_STALE_EVENT');
    expect(res1.clusterId).toBe(res2.clusterId);
  });

  test('Isolation of Blacklisted and High-Degree Hub Identifiers', () => {
    const dummyNodeA: IdentityNode = { id: 'email:unknown@domain.com', type: 'EMAIL', attributes: {}, createdAt: { wallTime: 100, logical: 0, nodeId: 'n1' }, updatedAt: { wallTime: 100, logical: 0, nodeId: 'n1' } };
    const dummyNodeB: IdentityNode = { id: 'crm:cust_123', type: 'CRM_ID', attributes: {}, createdAt: { wallTime: 100, logical: 0, nodeId: 'n1' }, updatedAt: { wallTime: 100, logical: 0, nodeId: 'n1' } };

    const edge: IdentityEdge = {
      id: 'edge_dummy',
      source: dummyNodeA.id,
      target: dummyNodeB.id,
      confidenceScore: 1.0,
      ruleId: 'BLACKLIST_RULE',
      sourceSystem: 'CRM',
      hlc: { wallTime: 200, logical: 0, nodeId: 'n1' },
      tombstoned: false
    };

    const result = engine.reconcileIdentityDelta(dummyNodeA, dummyNodeB, edge);
    expect(result.isQuarantined).toBe(true);
    expect(result.status).toBe('REJECTED_BLACKLIST');
  });
