## 4. Algorithms & Implementation Specification

### 4.1 Looker Studio Formula Lexer & AST Dependency Parser

Looker Studio formulas utilize an extended SQL-like syntax supporting conditional statements (`CASE WHEN`), string manipulations (`REGEXP_EXTRACT`, `CONCAT`), date arithmetic (`DATETIME_DIFF`), and aggregation wrappers (`SUM`, `COUNT_DISTINCT`).

```typescript
// src/drift/formula-parser.ts

export class LookerFormulaParser {
  private static readonly IDENTIFIER_REGEX = /(?:\[([^\]]+)\])|([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)/g;
  private static readonly RESERVED_KEYWORDS = new Set([
    'CASE', 'WHEN', 'THEN', 'ELSE', 'END', 'AND', 'OR', 'NOT',
    'IF', 'IFNULL', 'NULLIF', 'COALESCE', 'CONCAT', 'SUBSTR',
    'REGEXP_MATCH', 'REGEXP_EXTRACT', 'REGEXP_REPLACE',
    'SUM', 'AVG', 'MIN', 'MAX', 'COUNT', 'COUNT_DISTINCT',
    'DATETIME_ADD', 'DATETIME_SUB', 'DATETIME_DIFF', 'CURRENT_DATE',
    'EXTRACT', 'PARSE_DATE', 'FORMAT_DATE', 'CAST', 'AS', 'TRUE', 'FALSE', 'NULL'
  ]);

  /**
   * Extracts dependent field names from a Looker Studio calculated formula.
   * Handles both Bracketed identifiers `[Transaction Total]` and raw tokens `user_id`.
   */
  public static extractDependencies(formula: string, availableFieldNames: Set<string>): string[] {
    const dependencies = new Set<string>();
    let match: RegExpExecArray | null;

    // Reset regex index
    this.IDENTIFIER_REGEX.lastIndex = 0;

    while ((match = this.IDENTIFIER_REGEX.exec(formula)) !== null) {
      const bracketed = match[1];
      const raw = match[2];
      const token = bracketed || raw;

      if (!token) continue;

      const upperToken = token.toUpperCase();
      if (this.RESERVED_KEYWORDS.has(upperToken)) {
        continue;
      }

      // If bracketed notation is used, it is explicitly a field reference
      if (bracketed) {
        dependencies.add(bracketed.trim());
      } else if (availableFieldNames.has(token)) {
        dependencies.add(token);
      }
    }

    return Array.from(dependencies);
  }

  /**
   * Invariant Check: Verifies if formula uses aggregation over aggregation (Invalid in Looker).
   */
  public static validateAggregationHierarchy(
    formula: string,
    dependencyIsAggregatedMap: Map<string, boolean>
  ): { isValid: boolean; error?: string } {
    const hasOuterAggregation = /^(SUM|AVG|MIN|MAX|COUNT|COUNT_DISTINCT)\s*\(/i.test(formula.trim());

    if (hasOuterAggregation) {
      const deps = this.extractDependencies(formula, new Set(dependencyIsAggregatedMap.keys()));
      for (const dep of deps) {
        if (dependencyIsAggregatedMap.get(dep) === true) {
          return {
            isValid: false,
            error: `Invalid nested aggregation: Formula aggregates field '${dep}' which is already aggregated.`
          };
        }
      }
    }
    return { isValid: true };
  }
}
```

---

### 4.2 Upstream Schema Diff & Blast Radius Calculation Engine

```typescript
// src/drift/blast-radius-engine.ts

import {
  ReportDependencyGraph,
  BlastRadiusReport,
  FieldDriftDetail,
  DriftSeverity
} from './types.js';

export class BlastRadiusEngine {
  /**
   * Evaluates the full ripple effect of upstream schema shifts across the entire dependency DAG.
   */
  public static evaluateBlastRadius(
    graph: ReportDependencyGraph,
    currentUpstreamColumns: Record<string, { name: string; type: string }[]>
  ): BlastRadiusReport {
    const upstreamDrift: FieldDriftDetail[] = [];
    const directlyBrokenFields = new Set<string>();
    const transitiveBrokenFields = new Set<string>();

    // Step 1: Detect Upstream Column Deletions & Type Mutations
    for (const [sourceId, sourceMeta] of Object.entries(graph.upstreamSources)) {
      const activeColumns = currentUpstreamColumns[sourceId] || [];
      const activeColMap = new Map(activeColumns.map(c => [c.name.toLowerCase(), c.type]));

      for (const [cachedColName, cachedColMeta] of Object.entries(sourceMeta.columns)) {
        const currentType = activeColMap.get(cachedColName.toLowerCase());

        if (!currentType) {
          // Column completely dropped
          const matchingField = Object.values(graph.fields).find(
            f => f.sourceId === sourceId && f.name.toLowerCase() === cachedColName.toLowerCase()
          );

          const fieldId = matchingField ? matchingField.id : `raw_${sourceId}_${cachedColName}`;
          upstreamDrift.push({
            fieldId,
            fieldName: cachedColName,
            sourceId,
            changeType: 'REMOVED'
          });
          directlyBrokenFields.add(fieldId);
        } else if (currentType.toUpperCase() !== cachedColMeta.type.toUpperCase()) {
          // Data type mutated (e.g. INT64 -> STRING)
          const matchingField = Object.values(graph.fields).find(
            f => f.sourceId === sourceId && f.name.toLowerCase() === cachedColName.toLowerCase()
          );
          if (matchingField) {
            upstreamDrift.push({
              fieldId: matchingField.id,
              fieldName: cachedColName,
              sourceId,
              changeType: 'TYPE_MUTATION'
            });
            // Mark as potential direct break if coercion is lossy
            if (this.isLossyTypeCoercion(cachedColMeta.type, currentType)) {
              directlyBrokenFields.add(matchingField.id);
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }

    // Step 2: Transitive Closure traversal via Forward Adjacency
    const visited = new Set<string>();
    const queue: string[] = Array.from(directlyBrokenFields);

    while (queue.length > 0) {
      const currentBrokenId = queue.shift()!;
      if (visited.has(currentBrokenId)) continue;
      visited.add(currentBrokenId);

      const dependents = graph.forwardAdjacency[currentBrokenId] || [];
      for (const depId of dependents) {
        if (!directlyBrokenFields.has(depId) && !transitiveBrokenFields.has(depId)) {
          transitiveBrokenFields.add(depId);
          queue.push(depId);
        }
      }
    }

    // Step 3: Identify Affected Components & Compute Severity
    const allBrokenFieldIds = new Set([...directlyBrokenFields, ...transitiveBrokenFields]);
    const affectedComponents: BlastRadiusReport['affectedComponents'] = [];

    for (const [compId, comp] of Object.entries(graph.components)) {
      const componentFields = [
        ...comp.dimensions,
        ...comp.metrics,
        ...comp.filterFields,
        ...comp.sortFields
      ];

      const brokenUsed = componentFields.filter(fId => allBrokenFieldIds.has(fId));
      if (brokenUsed.length > 0) {
        affectedComponents.push({
          componentId: compId,
          componentType: comp.componentType,
          pageId: comp.pageId,
          pageTitle: comp.pageTitle,
          breakageReasons: brokenUsed.map(fId => `Field dependency broken: '${fId}'`),
          criticality: comp.pageTitle.toLowerCase().includes('exec') || comp.componentType === 'SCORECARD'
            ? 'TIER_1_EXECUTIVE'
            : 'TIER_2_OPERATIONAL'
        });
      }
    }

    const hasBreakingChanges = directlyBrokenFields.size > 0 || affectedComponents.length > 0;
    const maxSeverity: DriftSeverity = hasBreakingChanges
      ? 'CRITICAL_BREAK'
      : upstreamDrift.length > 0
      ? 'DEGRADED_COERCION'
      : 'COSMETIC_UNUSED';

    return {
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      reportId: graph.reportId,
      hasBreakingChanges,
      maxSeverity,
      upstreamDrift,
      directlyBrokenFields: Array.from(directlyBrokenFields),
      transitiveBrokenFields: Array.from(transitiveBrokenFields),
      affectedComponents,
      summary: {
        totalFieldsAffected: allBrokenFieldIds.size,
        totalChartsBroken: affectedComponents.length,
        affectedPagesCount: new Set(affectedComponents.map(c => c.pageId)).size
      }
    };
  }

  private static isLossyTypeCoercion(prev: string, curr: string): boolean {
    const p = prev.toUpperCase();
    const c = curr.toUpperCase();
    if ((p.includes('INT') || p.includes('FLOAT') || p.includes('NUMERIC')) && c.includes('STRING')) {
      return true; // Mathematical operations in calculated fields will fail
    }
    if (p.includes('DATE') && !c.includes('DATE')) {
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
```

---

## 5. Offline Sync, Caching & Storage Architecture

To prevent redundant browser automation calls and adhere to rate-limiting policies, metadata snapshots are persisted in a deterministic local cache directory.

```
/workspace/mcp-google-data-studio/
  └── .looker_cache/
      ├── schema_snapshots/
      │   ├── report_0b8a4f91_graph.json       # Serialized ReportDependencyGraph
      │   └── report_0b8a4f91_graph.sha256     # Hash for quick freshness check
      └── upstream_catalogs/
          └── bigquery_project_dataset_meta.json
```

### 5.1 Graph Serialization & Cache Invalidation

```typescript
// src/drift/cache-manager.ts

import * as fs from 'fs/promises';
import * as path from 'path';
import * as crypto from 'crypto';
import { ReportDependencyGraph } from './types.js';

export class ReportCacheManager {
  private static readonly CACHE_DIR = path.resolve(process.cwd(), '.looker_cache/schema_snapshots');

  public static async persistGraph(graph: ReportDependencyGraph): Promise<void> {
    await fs.mkdir(this.CACHE_DIR, { recursive: true });
    const content = JSON.stringify(graph, null, 2);
    const hash = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(content).digest('hex');

    const jsonPath = path.join(this.CACHE_DIR, `report_${graph.reportId}_graph.json`);
    const hashPath = path.join(this.CACHE_DIR, `report_${graph.reportId}_graph.sha256`);

    await fs.writeFile(jsonPath, content, 'utf-8');
    await fs.writeFile(hashPath, hash, 'utf-8');
  }

  public static async loadCachedGraph(reportId: string): Promise<ReportDependencyGraph | null> {
    try {
      const jsonPath = path.join(this.CACHE_DIR, `report_${reportId}_graph.json`);
      const content = await fs.readFile(jsonPath, 'utf-8');
      return JSON.parse(content) as ReportDependencyGraph;
    } catch {
      return null; // Cache miss
    }
  }
}
```

---

## 6. MCP Tool Integrations

The blast radius and schema drift engine will be exposed as three official MCP tools within [`src/tools/drift-tools.ts`](file:///workspace/mcp-google-data-studio/src/tools):

### 6.1 `looker_audit_schema_drift`
* **Purpose:** Queries upstream BigQuery / dbt catalog, diffs against the Looker report dependency graph, and produces a complete blast radius report.
* **Input Schema:**
  ```json
  {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "reportId": { "type": "string", "description": "The Looker Studio report GUID" },
      "strictMode": { "type": "boolean", "description": "If true, treats lossy type coercions as fatal errors" },
      "failThresholdCharts": { "type": "integer", "default": 0, "description": "Number of broken charts required to return exit code 1" }
    },
    "required": ["reportId"]
  }
  ```

### 6.2 `looker_simulate_formula_change`
* **Purpose:** Dry-runs a proposed formula or field rename without altering production, calculating exact downstream charts affected.
* **Input Schema:**
  ```json
  {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "reportId": { "type": "string" },
      "targetFieldId": { "type": "string" },
      "proposedFormula": { "type": "string" },
      "proposedName": { "type": "string" }
    },
    "required": ["reportId", "targetFieldId"]
  }
  ```

### 6.3 `looker_sync_report_manifest`
* **Purpose:** Uses CDP/Linking extraction to introspect all components, calculated formulas, and data blends in a report, refreshing the local `.looker_cache` DAG.

---

## 7. Edge Cases, Failure Modes & Safety Bounds

| Edge Case / Failure Mode | Risk Level | Mitigation Strategy |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Blended Data Join Field Mutation** | Critical | If a join key (e.g. `customer_id` across BigQuery and Google Sheets) is renamed in one source, the join model collapses silently. The DAG parser explicitly registers join keys as critical dependency anchors. |
| **Silent Type Coercion (`DATE` vs `DATETIME`)** | High | Looker Studio charts render blank when time-series dimensions encounter incompatible granularities without throwing explicit parser errors. The engine flags any datetime format changes as `DEGRADED_COERCION`. |
| **Nested Aggregation Invariant** | Medium | Users writing `SUM(Gross_Margin_Pct)` where `Gross_Margin_Pct` is already defined as `SUM(Profit)/SUM(Revenue)`. The formula parser runs aggregation hierarchy validation prior to deployment. |
| **Dynamic Date Range Dimensions** | Medium | Custom date fields used exclusively in page-level or report-level filter controls. The component parser indexes top-level report properties and page properties in addition to chart objects. |
| **Rate Limits on Upstream Data Catalog** | Low | Results from BigQuery `INFORMATION_SCHEMA` queries are cached with a 15-minute TTL to avoid exhausting cloud API quotas. |

---

## 8. Verification & CI/CD Gating Protocol

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["Git PR / dbt Migration"] --> B["mcp-google-data-studio audit"]
    B --> C{"Blast Radius > 0?"}
    C -->|Yes: Breaking| D["❌ Block PR with SARIF / Slack Alert"]
    C -->|No: Clean| E["✅ Approve Deployment & Sync Cache"]
```

### 8.1 Example CI/CD Action Step

```bash
# Example invocation in GitHub Actions / GitLab CI
node dist/index.js --tool looker_audit_schema_drift \
  --args '{"reportId": "a1b2c3d4-5678-90ab-cdef-1234567890ab", "failThresholdCharts": 0}'
```

---

## 9. Conclusion & Immediate Action Items

1. **Implement Formula Parser:** Add [`src/drift/formula-parser.ts`](file:///workspace/mcp-google-data-studio/src/drift) with complete Looker Studio keyword tokenization.
2. **Implement DAG Engine:** Build [`src/drift/blast-radius-engine.ts`](file:///workspace/mcp-google-data-studio/src/drift) to support forward adjacency traversal.
3. **Wire MCP Server Endpoints:** Register `looker_audit_schema_drift` and `looker_simulate_formula_change` in [`src/tools/`](file:///workspace/mcp-google-data-studio/src/tools) and export in [`src/index.ts`](file:///workspace/mcp-google-data-studio/src/index.ts).

