- **Personas Engaged:** Generative Dreamer (DMN, $T=0.92$) & Evaluative Arbiter (Prefrontal Zeno Critic, $T=0.50$)
- **Topic:** Key Architectural Bottlenecks, Scalability Patterns, and Production-Grade State Management in Manifest V3

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Speculative Question

### Speculative Question
> *In project `my-analyzer-extension`, what are the key architectural bottlenecks and scalability patterns for its tech stack (Manifest V3, Content/Injected Scripts, Service Worker, CDP/Network Interception, Sidepanel UI, and AI LLM Engine)?*

### Abstract
`my-analyzer-extension` operates at the intersection of high-frequency DOM/Network telemetry interception and real-time LLM cognitive synthesis. The current architecture suffers from five critical failure modes:
1. **Service Worker State Evaporation:** MV3 service worker lifecycle teardowns purge global in-memory maps (`networkMonitoring`, `domainData`, `cdpPayloadData`).
2. **IPC Message Flooding & Bridge Saturation:** Unthrottled `window.postMessage` serialization across injected scripts, isolated content scripts, and extension ports creates event loop lag on high-throughput e-commerce single-page apps (SPAs).
3. **CDP Debugger Overhead & Tab Invasiveness:** Continuous `chrome.debugger` attachment introduces serialization bottlenecks, intrusive browser UI warnings, and debugger detach crashes during fast navigations.
4. **LLM Context Explosion & Cost/Latency Drift:** Raw dumps of DataLayer events, CDP network trees, and cookie vectors directly into Gemini/Claude APIs exhaust context windows and cause multi-second latency spikes.
5. **Storage Quota & Serialization Blockades:** Monolithic JSON serialization of `domainData` directly to `chrome.storage.local` triggers I/O thrashing and memory spikes.

This RFC defines a high-performance, fault-tolerant reactive architecture utilizing **Bounded Circular Ring Buffers**, **Three-Tier Ephemeral/Persistent Storage**, **Offscreen Document Worker Pools**, and a **Semantic LLM Context Distillation Pipeline**.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph Execution_Context_MainWorld["Main World (Target Page)"]
        Inj["injected.js (Monkey-patched APIs)"]
        DL["DataLayer Hooks / XHR / Fetch"]
        Inj -->|Debounced Ring Buffer| PostMsg["window.postMessage (Structured Clones)"]
    end

    subgraph Content_Script_Boundary["Isolated World"]
        CS["content.js (Bridge Validator)"]
        PostMsg -->|Port Stream| CS
    end

    subgraph Service_Worker_MV3["Background Service Worker (MV3)"]
        CS -->|chrome.runtime.Port| Dispatcher["Telemetry Event Bus & Throttle"]
        SW_State["Session Cache (chrome.storage.session)"]
        Dispatcher <--> SW_State
        Dispatcher --> TieredStorage["Three-Tier Storage Engine"]
    end

    subgraph Offscreen_Worker_Subsystem["Offscreen Document / Workers"]
        TieredStorage --> IndexedDB["IndexedDB (Chunked Blob Stores)"]
        Dispatcher --> AST_Worker["Regex/Trie SDK Classifier & Offscreen Decompressor"]
    end

    subgraph AI_Distillation_Engine["LLM Cognitive Engine"]
        AST_Worker --> ContextCompressor["Semantic Context Distiller (Lossy Token Reduction)"]
        ContextCompressor --> LLM["Gemini 2.5 / Claude 3.5 API"]
    end

    subgraph Presentation_Layer["UI Subsystem"]
        TieredStorage --> SidePanel["sidepanel.js / panel.js (Virtual DOM / Infinite Scroll)"]
