## 5. Concrete Data Structures & Ingestion Algorithms

### 5.1. Bounded LRU + IndexedDB Stale-While-Revalidate Engine (`@onmartech/social-cms`)

To prevent API rate-limiting and browser storage quota exceptions, social feed ingestion must follow a multi-tier cache hierarchy: Memory (L1) -> IndexedDB (L2) -> Network (L3).

```
   Incoming Request: getFeed(channelId)
            │
            ▼
    [ L1: Memory Cache (LRU) ] ───(Hit & Fresh)───> Return Instant Memory Feed
            │ (Miss / Stale)
            ▼
    [ L2: IndexedDB Storage  ] ───(Hit & Valid)───> Yield Stale Data to UI
            │                                             │ (Background Revalidate)
            │ (Miss)                                      ▼
            └───────────────────────────────────> [ L3: Network Fetch / Adapter ]
                                                          │
                                                    (Success)
                                                          │
                                                    ┌─────┴────────────────┐
                                                    ▼                      ▼
                                            Update L1 & L2         Emit Updated Feed
```

#### Algorithm: Stale-While-Revalidate with Exponential Jittered Backoff

```typescript
/**
 * Core Cache Metadata & Item Structure
 */
export interface CacheEntry<T> {
  key: string;
  data: T;
  timestamp: number;
  ttlMs: number;
  staleAfterMs: number;
  etag?: string;
  version: number;
}

export interface IngestionOptions {
  ttlMs?: number;         // Max shelf-life (e.g. 24h)
  staleAfterMs?: number;  // SWR revalidation threshold (e.g. 5m)
  maxRetries?: number;
  baseDelayMs?: number;
}

export class ResilientFeedStore {
  private memoryCache = new Map<string, CacheEntry<unknown>>();
  private maxMemorySize = 100;

  constructor(private dbName = 'OnmartechSocialDB', private storeName = 'feeds') {}

  /**
   * Deterministic SWR Ingestion
   */
  async getOrFetch<T>(
    key: string,
    fetcher: (etag?: string) => Promise<{ data: T; etag?: string }>,
    opts: IngestionOptions = {}
  ): Promise<{ data: T; fromCache: boolean; isStale: boolean }> {
    const ttlMs = opts.ttlMs ?? 86400000;          // 24 hours
    const staleAfterMs = opts.staleAfterMs ?? 300000; // 5 minutes
    const now = Date.now();

    // 1. Check L1 Memory Cache
    let cached = this.memoryCache.get(key) as CacheEntry<T> | undefined;

    // 2. Check L2 IndexedDB if missing in L1
    if (!cached) {
      cached = await this.readIndexedDB<T>(key);
      if (cached) {
        this.writeMemoryCache(key, cached);
      }
    }

    if (cached) {
      const age = now - cached.timestamp;
      const isExpired = age > cached.ttlMs;
      const isStale = age > cached.staleAfterMs;

      if (!isExpired) {
        if (isStale) {
          // Trigger asynchronous background revalidation
          this.revalidateInBackground(key, fetcher, cached.etag, ttlMs, staleAfterMs);
        }
        return { data: cached.data, fromCache: true, isStale };
      }
    }

    // 3. Mandatory Fresh Network Ingestion with Backoff
    const freshData = await this.fetchWithBackoff(fetcher, cached?.etag, opts.maxRetries ?? 3, opts.baseDelayMs ?? 500);
    const entry: CacheEntry<T> = {
      key,
      data: freshData.data,
      timestamp: now,
      ttlMs,
      staleAfterMs,
      etag: freshData.etag,
      version: 1,
    };

    this.writeMemoryCache(key, entry);
    await this.writeIndexedDB(key, entry);

    return { data: freshData.data, fromCache: false, isStale: false };
  }

  private async fetchWithBackoff<T>(
    fetcher: (etag?: string) => Promise<{ data: T; etag?: string }>,
    etag: string | undefined,
    retries: number,
    delayMs: number
  ): Promise<{ data: T; etag?: string }> {
    try {
      return await fetcher(etag);
    } catch (err) {
      if (retries <= 0) throw err;
      // Exponential backoff with Full Jitter: sleep = rand(0, min(cap, base * 2^attempt))
      const jitter = Math.random() * (delayMs * 2);
      await new Promise((res) => setTimeout(res, jitter));
      return this.fetchWithBackoff(fetcher, etag, retries - 1, delayMs * 2);
    }
  }

  private writeMemoryCache(key: string, entry: CacheEntry<unknown>): void {
    if (this.memoryCache.size >= this.maxMemorySize) {
      // LRU Eviction: Remove oldest key
      const firstKey = this.memoryCache.keys().next().value;
      if (firstKey) this.memoryCache.delete(firstKey);
    }
    this.memoryCache.set(key, entry);
  }

  private async readIndexedDB<T>(key: string): Promise<CacheEntry<T> | undefined> {
    if (typeof window === 'undefined' || !window.indexedDB) return undefined;
    return new Promise((resolve) => {
      const req = window.indexedDB.open(this.dbName, 1);
      req.onupgradeneeded = () => req.result.createObjectStore(this.storeName, { keyPath: 'key' });
      req.onsuccess = () => {
        const tx = req.result.transaction(this.storeName, 'readonly');
        const store = tx.objectStore(this.storeName);
        const getReq = store.get(key);
        getReq.onsuccess = () => resolve(getReq.result as CacheEntry<T>);
        getReq.onerror = () => resolve(undefined);
      };
      req.onerror = () => resolve(undefined);
    });
  }

  private async writeIndexedDB(key: string, entry: CacheEntry<unknown>): Promise<void> {
    if (typeof window === 'undefined' || !window.indexedDB) return;
    return new Promise((resolve) => {
      const req = window.indexedDB.open(this.dbName, 1);
      req.onsuccess = () => {
        const tx = req.result.transaction(this.storeName, 'readwrite');
        const store = tx.objectStore(this.storeName);
        store.put(entry);
        tx.oncomplete = () => resolve();
        tx.onerror = () => resolve();
      };
      req.onerror = () => resolve();
    });
  }

  private revalidateInBackground<T>(
    key: string,
    fetcher: (etag?: string) => Promise<{ data: T; etag?: string }>,
    etag: string | undefined,
    ttlMs: number,
    staleAfterMs: number
  ): void {
    this.fetchWithBackoff(fetcher, etag, 2, 1000)
      .then((fresh) => {
        const entry: CacheEntry<T> = {
          key,
          data: fresh.data,
          timestamp: Date.now(),
          ttlMs,
          staleAfterMs,
          etag: fresh.etag,
          version: 1,
        };
        this.writeMemoryCache(key, entry);
        this.writeIndexedDB(key, entry);
      })
      .catch((err) => {
        console.warn(`[SocialCMS] Background revalidation failed for ${key}:`, err);
      });
  }
}
```

---

## 6. Hybrid SSR / RSC Session Bridge for `@onmartech/auth`

To support both Next.js App Router Server Components (RSC) and interactive client hooks, `@onmartech/auth` is split into dual submodules:
1. `@onmartech/auth/client`: Firebase Auth SDK state, `useAuth()`, Google/Email popup triggers.
2. `@onmartech/auth/server`: Lightweight JWT / Session Cookie verification using `jose` or `firebase-admin` (edge-compatible without bundling heavy client Firebase libraries).

```typescript
// packages/auth/src/server/session.ts
import { jwtVerify, createRemoteJWKSet } from 'jose';

const FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID || 'onmartech';
const JWKS = createRemoteJWKSet(
  new URL('https://www.googleapis.com/service_accounts/v1/jwk/securetoken@system.gserviceaccount.com')
);

export interface DecodedAuthSession {
  uid: string;
  email?: string;
  role?: string;
  exp: number;
}

export async function verifySessionCookie(token: string): Promise<DecodedAuthSession | null> {
  try {
    const { payload } = await jwtVerify(token, JWKS, {
      issuer: `https://securetoken.google.com/${FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID}`,
      audience: FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID,
    });

    return {
      uid: payload.sub as string,
      email: payload.email as string | undefined,
      role: (payload.role as string) || 'user',
      exp: payload.exp as number,
    };
  } catch (error) {
    return null;
  }
}
```

---

## 7. AI-Ready Agent Primitives (Google cognitive_agent SDK Alignment)

As onmartech transitions toward **Agent as a Service (AaaS)**, packages must expose structured interfaces and deterministic Zod schemas so that AGY agents can programmatically manipulate UI states, trigger WhatsApp workflows, and publish content without parsing raw React components.

```typescript
// packages/types/src/agent-schemas.ts
import { z } from 'zod';

export const WhatsAppMessageActionSchema = z.object({
  recipientPhone: z.string().regex(/^\+?[1-9]\d{1,14}$/, 'Invalid E.164 phone format'),
  templateId: z.string().min(1),
  templateParams: z.record(z.string()),
  fallbackWaMeUrl: z.string().url(),
});

export const SocialPublishActionSchema = z.object({
  targetPlatforms: z.array(z.enum(['telegram', 'instagram', 'sanity'])),
  title: z.string().min(1).max(255),
  contentMarkdown: z.string(),
  mediaUrls: z.array(z.string().url()).max(10),
  scheduleTime: z.string().datetime().optional(),
});

export type WhatsAppMessageAction = z.infer<typeof WhatsAppMessageActionSchema>;
export type SocialPublishAction = z.infer<typeof SocialPublishActionSchema>;
```

---

## 8. Edge Cases, Safety Bounds, & Failure Recovery

| Scenario / Edge Case | Failure Mode | Architectural Defense & Safety Bound |
|---|---|---|
| **Storage Quota Exceeded** | `localStorage.setItem` throws `QuotaExceededError` on large images. | IndexedDB primary store + automatic LRU pruning of payloads older than 7 days. |
| **Telegram Rate Limit (HTTP 429)** | Subsequent site visitors get blank social widgets. | SWR engine serves stale cached entries indefinitely with `isStale: true` until the API resets. |
| **RSC Component Import** | Importing `@onmartech/ui` components into server-only files. | `tsup` inserts `'use client'` directive to root bundles; `tokens` are exported as pure pure JSON/objects via `@onmartech/ui/tokens`. |
| **Canvas Tree-Shaking Failure** | Client sites importing simple buttons receive 200KB `@xyflow` bundle. | Subpath separation (`@onmartech/ui/canvas`), isolating React Flow into a dedicated entrypoint. |
| **Firebase Auth Token Expiry** | SSR page render fails during token refresh. | Graceful fallback to unauthenticated state with edge redirect to `/login` via HTTP-only cookie. |

---

## 9. Implementation Roadmap & Verification Milestones

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    M1["Milestone 1:<br/>Tooling & Bundler Hardening<br/>(tsup, ESM/CJS, DTS)"] --> M2["Milestone 2:<br/>Subpath Splitting &<br/>Canvas Isolation"]
    M2 --> M3["Milestone 3:<br/>Social-CMS Resilience &<br/>IndexedDB Engine"]
    M3 --> M4["Milestone 4:<br/>Auth RSC Bridge &<br/>cognitive_agent Agent Schemas"]
```

### Milestone 1: Tooling & Build Hardening (Week 1)
- Install and configure `tsup` across all packages in `packages/*`.
- Replace `"main": "./src/index.ts"` with explicit `"exports"` maps targeting `./dist`.
- Configure `turbo.json` build outputs to cache `./dist/**`.
- Eliminate `transpilePackages` requirement in `onmartech-web`, `fronti-web`, and `quantum-portal-web`.

### Milestone 2: Subpath Splitting & Bundle Optimization (Week 2)
- Extract `@xyflow/react` from core `@onmartech/ui` into `@onmartech/ui/canvas`.
- Verify bundle sizes using `bundle-analyzer`: Ensure `@onmartech/ui` root import stays below **12KB gzipped**.
- Ensure design tokens in `@onmartech/ui/tokens` are free of any DOM/React runtime dependencies.

### Milestone 3: Social CMS Resilience (Week 3)
- Integrate `ResilientFeedStore` into `@onmartech/social-cms`.
- Implement automated Telegram and Instagram rate-limit recovery with ETag matching.
- Add unit tests verifying IndexedDB fallback when network is disconnected.

### Milestone 4: Auth Server Separation & Agent Integration (Week 4)
- Publish `@onmartech/auth/server` with edge-compatible JOSE token verification.
- Export standard Zod schemas in `@onmartech/types` for direct integration with Google cognitive_agent SDK agents (`@onmartech/ai-agent`).
- Run Changeset release `0.2.0` to GitHub Packages registry.

